cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this technical tutorial or software, cite the archived release associated with the repository record."
title: "When raw microscopy data are gone: a responsible workflow for auditing legacy bioimage analyses"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Montefusco-Pereira"
    given-names: "Carlos Victor"
version: "0.1.0-dev"
date-released: "2026-08-01"
repository-code: "https://github.com/camontefusco/legacy-bioimage-audit"
abstract: >-
  Technical tutorial and historical reconstruction for auditing legacy
  bioimage analyses when raw acquisitions or labels are unavailable. The
  package demonstrates provenance, sensitivity, quality control, experimental
  units, and responsible stopping rules. It is not a validated biological
  treatment-effect pipeline.
keywords:
  - bioimage analysis
  - reproducibility
  - Pseudomonas aeruginosa
  - microscopy
license: MIT
